<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I25a23e270bae5f4fa7afffc6b834ce94c1433436" commit="78d74a5134603187745f1c114caaeed084913b1e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: HACK: vop0 (big) pixel clock owns VPLL, nobody else uses  There are a few possible problems with the 'normal' VOP clk tree: 1. At the whim of firmware, it's possible that VPLL will be initialized to something that is a multiple of our chosen pixel clock (266666 MHz). At the whim of common clock framework it's possible that VPLL will be chosen as the parent clock of the little VOP and be used by eDP. Now when we plug into type C then we'll want to change VPLL. Common clock framework is not currently smart enough to know that it should reparent the little VOP to CPLL / GPLL in this case. Instead the eDP pixel clock will be unexpectedly changed. Note that there are some &quot;whims&quot; there, but generally I don't like relying on un-guaranteed behavior.  2. Even if little vop gets cpll / gpll (YAY), the common clock framework could (on a whim) decide to also point the big VOP to cpll / gpll, maybe because you plug into a external display that happens to have pixel clock that can be made from cpll / gpll. Then you might change your display mode. Rather than reparent the big VOP back to vpll, the CCF might (on a whim) decide to change the rate of CPLL / GPLL, which would be a terrible idea. To summarize: the CCF has too much &quot;automatic&quot; behavior if you've got both CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT and you allow auto-remuxing (the default).  It's going to bite us unless we do something to make sure that only the expected parents are used.  Mark dummy for all the PLL which we don't want to assign to someone. That will give VPLL to big VOP. Little VOP will dynamically switch between CPLL and GPLL depending on the requested pixel clock.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52872 TEST=Check DP and eDP display  Change-Id: I25a23e270bae5f4fa7afffc6b834ce94c1433436 Signed-off-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362820 Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362820" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="31" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/362820/31" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I5d11ae30a1bdc7f7fb580726249e7944689ad759" commit="dbd7816d03b531ee76e1438b0f62075f913c1d30" commit_message="CHROMIUM: HACK: clk: rockchip: don't use frac clocks for VOP on rk3399  In order to get low jitter on the pixel clock, testing indicates that the fractional divider that can be a source to the VOPs needs to be _at least_ &quot;divide by 20&quot;.  Even with a source PLL of 2.4 GHz that gives us a maximum pixel clock of 120 MHz.  This is not enough to support all pixel clocks that we expect to need.  In theory we could be dynamic and use the fractional clock to make some of the stranger clock frequencies that are &lt; 120 MHz.  That would be ideal, but at the moment it's pretty hard because:  1. CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT doesn't work on fractional clocks. See http://crosreview.com/371641  2. We'd need to integrate the concept of jitter into the Rockchip clock framework and VOP client (maybe using clk_get_accuracy?) so we could set jitter requirements for the pixel clock and make sure that the fraction clock isn't configured in a way to give too much jitter.  The above is a very difficult task.  Until all that is done, let's simply hack out the connection to the fractional clock which will force common clock framework to just never use it.  Change-Id: I5d11ae30a1bdc7f7fb580726249e7944689ad759 Signed-off-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/370779 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="370779" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="16" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/79/370779/16" remote="cros" total_fail_count="6"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie30f0679387550b1fd446a25734d8c5c436aba66" commit="fb8aa32e82f7945676d382a0ad3fd7f0bfd80b1e" commit_message="autotest: Remove power_SuspendShutdown.  Remove the power_SuspendShutdown test. This functionality is already covered by the power_manager package's unit tests.  BUG=chromium:631504 TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=I42d38cce87903c261a7f7ea8291f6ed71fb8a261  Change-Id: Ie30f0679387550b1fd446a25734d8c5c436aba66 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383751 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383751" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/51/383751/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I42d38cce87903c261a7f7ea8291f6ed71fb8a261" commit="3783b196d92d6dce9d1550e53e9871e152296fae" commit_message="autotest-server-tests: Unlist power_SuspendShutdown.  Unlist the power_SuspendShutdown test. This functionality is already covered by the power_manager package's unit tests.  BUG=chromium:631504 TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=Ie30f0679387550b1fd446a25734d8c5c436aba66  Change-Id: I42d38cce87903c261a7f7ea8291f6ed71fb8a261 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383712 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383712" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/12/383712/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibab7ad30d5f1ae9917b46b40d6f2800ef19e52dd" commit="582b634cbe3ba58d6c6e54be18dd2746fe6741f4" commit_message="bd99955: Add support for power save mode.  The BD99956 charger has a power save mode that it can enter once VBUS or VCC is removed.  This commit adds an optional config option that can be used to select the power save mode:    CONFIG_BD99955_POWER_SAVE_MODE  By default, no power save mode will be enabled.  However, a board can device what level of power savings they wish to use.  The levels are the following:  BD99955_PWR_SAVE_LOW /* BGATE ON w/ PROCHOT# monitored only system                       * voltage. */  BD99955_PWR_SAVE_MED /* BGATE ON w/ PROCHOT# monitored only system                       * voltage every 1ms. */  BD99955_PWR_SAVE_HIGH /* BGATE ON w/o PROCHOT# monitoring. */  BD99955_PWR_SAVE_MAX  /* BGATE OFF */  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55631 BRANCH=kevin TEST=make -j buildall  Change-Id: Ibab7ad30d5f1ae9917b46b40d6f2800ef19e52dd Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/382877 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="382877" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/77/382877/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I05274a770b35c981e0541d8f79f66b81ffb4d153" commit="8847b2bc4b54a937e76984197d0de9f924b0418d" commit_message="kevin: bd99955: Enable power save mode.  For kevin, we are not using the PROCHOT# signal for the charger so we can enable a power save mode.  This commit will leave BGATE on but without monitoring the PROCHOT# signal.  When VBUS or VCC is removed from the charger, the charger will enter this power save mode.  It will return to normal functionality when VBUS or VCC is applied.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55631 BRANCH=kevin TEST=Flash kevin; Verify we can still charge; Verify that power consumption is less with this patch applied than without.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:382877  Change-Id: I05274a770b35c981e0541d8f79f66b81ffb4d153 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383391 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383391" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/91/383391/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If9844d03ea082252a2d12a83658c982172a93589" commit="58e117544424f51b76a5f384a1110deca89edde4" commit_message="[autotest] Fix lint error in servo.py  BUG=None TEST=no more lint errors uploading changes to servo.py!  Change-Id: If9844d03ea082252a2d12a83658c982172a93589 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383771 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383771" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/71/383771/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2989e1cd139a6a851dec68e3183117db71775df3" commit="06573cf705a402837973987aa5b5455e850922c3" commit_message="[toolchain builders] Remove kernel tests from llvm builders.  Since the kernel is not being built with LLVM, there is no need to run the kernel HWTests on the LLVM buildbots.  This removes them. Also creates a minimal set of tests for use on some boards.  BUG=chromium:645246 TEST=ran ./run_tests successfully.  Change-Id: I2989e1cd139a6a851dec68e3183117db71775df3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383136 Commit-Ready: Caroline Tice &lt;cmtice@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Caroline Tice &lt;cmtice@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383136" owner_email="cmtice@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/36/383136/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I13765dc8588661a949ed214e0d7c5c9b5a55aa4a" commit="21758b7d06b76e605a0451d194bac8df18a0ff47" commit_message="cryptohome: fix race for InitializeTpmComplete and mount_thread  In Service::Initialize(), tpm initialization that runs in a parallel thread is started before a call to mount_thread_.Start(). When the tpm initialization completes, it posts a task to a MessageLoop of mount_thread_. If mount_thread_ is not started by then, we get a null pointer dereference.  BUG=b:31371846 TEST=unittests (new added: ServiceTestNotInitialized.CheckTpmInitRace)  Change-Id: I13765dc8588661a949ed214e0d7c5c9b5a55aa4a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383233 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail